Our Old Chicago restaurants place significant emphasis on staff training, with a special
emphasis on the responsible service of alcohol beverages.Eachserver, at the time of
opening, isrequired tohave successfully completed the standardized testin the National
Restaurant Association'scertified Ser v Safe Alcohol Program.The Se rv Safe Alcohol course
consists of class instruction employing training videos as well as a written guide and
generally takes 4-5 hours to complete including administration of the exam.The Serv Safe
Alcohol course includes comprehensive coverage of areas such as“Alcohol, Law, and Your
Responsibility,”“Recognizing and Preventing Intoxication，”“Checking Identification,”and
“Handing Difficult Situations.”The program further allows for our trainers to incorporate
state and/or local specific issues or restrictions such as hours of service, record keeping
requirements, andright of entry.Inaddition, Old Chicagois a member of theBARS
PROGRAM(Being A Responsible Server).BARS(an independently owned and operated
